<section class="story">
  <div class="container story__grid">
    <figure class="media media--4x3">
      {% img "assets/images/projects/gsx/default.JPG", "GSX-1 wireframe sculpture" %}
    </figure>

    <div class="story__content">
      <h2 class="story__title">Object First</h2>
      <p class="story__text">
        GSX-1 started as a small wireframe sculpture inspired by electronics-as-art builds, where
        the circuit and the structure are part of the same visual language.
      </p>
      <p class="story__text">
        The challenge was to keep the wiring tidy enough to feel intentional while still fitting
        the microcontroller, GPS-related modules and display elements into a very small footprint.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story story--reverse">
  <div class="container story__grid">
    <figure class="media media--4x3">
      {% img "assets/images/projects/gsx/gpscloseup.JPG", "GSX-1 close-up electronics" %}
    </figure>

    <div class="story__content">
      <h2 class="story__title">Electronics</h2>
      <p class="story__text">
        I built the wiring scheme around an RP2040-based controller and wrote the control logic in
        C++ through the Arduino toolchain.
      </p>
      <p class="story__text">
        The focus was not only making it work, but also making the signal routing and physical
        assembly readable when viewed up close.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story">
  <div class="container story__grid">
    <figure class="media media--4x3">
      {% img "assets/images/projects/gsx/splash.JPG", "GSX-1 display splash screen" %}
    </figure>

    <div class="story__content">
      <h2 class="story__title">Interface</h2>
      <p class="story__text">
        The visible software layer is intentionally minimal: a small interface, clean startup
        behavior and enough feedback to make the object feel alive without turning it into a gadget demo.
      </p>
      <p class="story__text">
        This made the project a useful exercise in balancing technical density with visual restraint.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

